-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-ingredient-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: var(--meadow-accent-color);\">Ingredients</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredients\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">ounce</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Dried wakame seaweed</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">2</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoons</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Rice vinegar</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">tablespoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Soy sauce</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Sesame oil</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Sugar</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-unit\">teaspoon</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Toasted sesame seeds</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">1</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Green onion</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Thinly sliced</span></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\" data-uid=\"-1\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-amount\">Pinch</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-name\">Red pepper flakes</span>&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes wprm-recipe-ingredient-notes-faded\">Optional</span></li></ul></div></div></div>\n      <div id=\"recipe-12906-equipment\" class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"12906\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-equipment-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Equipment</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-internal-container wprm-internal-container-equipment wprm-expandable-container wprm-expandable-expanded\" style=\"\"><div class=\"wprm-internal-container-toggle\"><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-show\" aria-label=\"Show Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,9.5 8,5 12.5,9.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a><a role=\"button\" aria-expanded=\"true\" class=\"wprm-expandable-button wprm-expandable-button-hide\" aria-label=\"Hide Section\"><span class=\"wprm-recipe-icon wprm-collapsible-icon\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\"><g class=\"nc-icon-wrapper\" stroke-width=\"1\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#333333\" stroke-miterlimit=\"10\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><polyline points=\"3.5,6.5 8,11 12.5,6.5 \"></polyline></g></svg></span> </a></div><ul class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment wprm-recipe-equipment-list\"><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;border-bottom: 1px solid var(--meadow-list-border-color);padding-bottom: 5px;margin-bottom: 5px;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 Bowl&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For soaking seaweed and mixing dressing</span></div></li><li class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-item\" style=\"list-style-type: none;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-name\">1 whisk&#32;<span class=\"wprm-recipe-equipment-notes wprm-recipe-equipment-notes-normal\">For mixing dressing</span></div></li></ul></div></div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"wprm-layout-column wprm-column-width-50 meadow-main-right\">\n      <div id=\"recipe-12906-instructions\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions-container wprm-recipe-12906-instructions-container wprm-block-text-normal\" data-recipe=\"12906\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-instructions-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-spacer wprm-header-has-actions\" style=\"\">Method<div class=\"wprm-decoration-spacer\"></div>&nbsp;</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-group\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-group-name wprm-recipe-instruction-group-name wprm-block-text-bold\" style=\"color: #000000;\">Instructions</div><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 5px;\"></div><ol class=\"wprm-recipe-instructions\"><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12906-step-0-0\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 1: Soak the Seaweed &#8211; Start by soaking the dried wakame seaweed in a bowl of cold water. Let it sit for 5–10 minutes until it becomes rehydrated and tender. Once ready, drain the seaweed and gently squeeze out any excess water.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12906-step-0-1\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 2: Make the Dressing &#8211; In a separate bowl, whisk together rice vinegar, soy sauce, sesame oil, sugar, and red pepper flakes if you like a little heat. This dressing will bring all the flavors together beautifully!</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12906-step-0-2\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 3: Combine Ingredients &#8211; Add the drained seaweed and sliced green onion to the bowl with the dressing. Toss everything gently to ensure the seaweed is evenly coated with the delicious mixture.</span></div></li><li id=\"wprm-recipe-12906-step-0-3\" class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction\" style=\"list-style-type: decimal;\"><div class=\"wprm-recipe-instruction-text\" style=\"margin-bottom: 10px;\"><span style=\"display: block;\">Step 4: Serve and Enjoy &#8211; Finally, sprinkle the salad with toasted sesame seeds for that extra crunch. Serve it chilled or at room temperature, and enjoy your refreshing seaweed salad!</span></div></li></ol></div></div>\n      \n      \n      <div id=\"recipe-12906-notes\" class=\"wprm-recipe-notes-container wprm-block-text-normal\"><h3 class=\"wprm-recipe-header wprm-recipe-notes-header wprm-block-text-bold wprm-align-left wprm-header-decoration-none\" style=\"\">Notes</h3><div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 15px;\"></div><div class=\"wprm-recipe-notes\"><table>\n<tr>\n<th>Nutrient</th>\n<th>Amount per Serving</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Calories</td>\n<td>45</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Fat</td>\n<td>2g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Protein</td>\n<td>3g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Carbs</td>\n<td>6g</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sugar</td>\n<td>1g</td>\n</tr>\n</table></div></div>\n      <div class=\"wprm-spacer\" style=\"height: 40px;\"></div>\n      \n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div></div></div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"ingredients\"><strong>Ingredients</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Gather these simple ingredients for a delightful <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seaweed\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">seaweed </a>salad!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Ingredients-for-Seaweed-Salad.webp\" alt=\"Ingredients for seaweed salad displayed on a kitchen table.\" class=\"wp-image-12904\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Ingredients-for-Seaweed-Salad.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Ingredients-for-Seaweed-Salad-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Dried wakame seaweed</strong> – 1 ounce</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Rice vinegar</strong> – 2 tablespoons</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Soy sauce</strong> – 1 tablespoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sesame oil</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Sugar</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Toasted sesame seeds</strong> – 1 teaspoon</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Green onion</strong> – 1, thinly sliced</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Red pepper flakes</strong> – Pinch (optional)</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-make-seaweed-salad\"><strong>How to Make Seaweed Salad</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This delightful seaweed salad is not only quick to prepare but also a healthy addition to your meals. With a preparation time of just 10 minutes and no cooking time required, you can whip this up in no time. Allow it to chill for a few minutes for the flavors to meld, making it a perfect side dish!</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image aligncenter size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"400\" height=\"533\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Step-by-Step-Seaweed-Salad-Preparation.webp\" alt=\"Four-part image showing the preparation steps for seaweed salad, including soaking seaweed, making dressing, combining ingredients, and serving the salad.\" class=\"wp-image-12905\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Step-by-Step-Seaweed-Salad-Preparation.webp 400w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Step-by-Step-Seaweed-Salad-Preparation-225x300.webp 225w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px\" /></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 1: Soak the Seaweed</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Start by soaking the dried wakame seaweed in a bowl of cold water. Let it sit for 5–10 minutes until it becomes rehydrated and tender. Once ready, drain the seaweed and gently squeeze out any excess water.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 2: Make the Dressing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a separate bowl, whisk together rice vinegar, soy sauce, sesame oil, sugar, and red pepper flakes if you like a little heat. This dressing will bring all the flavors together beautifully!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 3: Combine Ingredients</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Add the drained seaweed and sliced green onion to the bowl with the dressing. Toss everything gently to ensure the seaweed is evenly coated with the delicious mixture.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Step 4: Serve and Enjoy</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Finally, sprinkle the salad with toasted sesame seeds for that extra crunch. Serve it chilled or at room temperature, and enjoy your refreshing seaweed salad!</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"recipe-snapshot\"><strong>Recipe Snapshot</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Details</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Category</td><td>Salad</td></tr><tr><td>Cuisine</td><td>Japanese</td></tr><tr><td>Prep Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Cook Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Extra Time</td><td>0 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Total Time</td><td>10 minutes</td></tr><tr><td>Dietary</td><td>Low-calorie</td></tr><tr><td>Serves</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>Best Served</td><td>Chilled or at room temperature</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"pro-tips-for-making-seaweed-salad\"><strong>Pro Tips for Making seaweed salad</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Soak the seaweed in cold water for 10-15 minutes for the best texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Add a splash of rice vinegar for a tangy kick.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Incorporate sesame seeds for added crunch and flavor.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Experiment with different seaweed types for unique tastes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Chill the salad before serving for a refreshing experience.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"how-to-serve-this-seaweed-salad\"><strong>How to Serve this seaweed salad</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Serve chilled as a refreshing appetizer.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Pair with grilled chicken or tofu for a balanced meal.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Top with sesame seeds for added crunch.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Mix into sushi rolls for a flavorful twist.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Enjoy as a side dish with rice or quinoa bowls.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Garnish with sliced cucumbers and radishes for extra freshness.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"make-ahead-and-storage\"><strong>Make Ahead and Storage</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Storing and enjoying your seaweed salad later is easy!</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Storing Leftovers</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Transfer leftovers to an airtight container.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Refrigerate within two hours of serving.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consume within 2-3 days for best flavor.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Freezing</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Seaweed salad is best enjoyed fresh, but can be frozen.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Place in a freezer-safe container or bag.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Remove as much air as possible to prevent freezer burn.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use within 1-2 months for optimal quality.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Reheating</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Thaw in the refrigerator overnight before reheating.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Gently toss with a little sesame oil to refresh flavors.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Avoid microwaving to maintain texture.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Serve chilled or at room temperature for best taste.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Explore more easy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/breakfast/\"><strong>breakfast</strong></a> recipes, quick <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/lunch/\"><strong>lunch</strong></a> ideas, cozy <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dinner/\"><strong>dinner</strong></a> meals, tasty <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/snacks/\"><strong>snacks</strong></a>, and delightful <a href=\"https://www.grandmarecipe.com/category/dessert/\"><strong>dessert</strong></a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"fa-qs\"><strong>FAQs</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Here’s a helpful FAQ about this recipe:</p>\n\n\n<div id=\"rank-math-faq\" class=\"rank-math-block\">\n<div class=\"rank-math-list \">\n<div id=\"faq-question-1\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>1. What does seaweed salad have in it?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Seaweed salad typically includes a variety of seaweeds, such as wakame, along with ingredients like sesame oil, soy sauce, rice vinegar, and sometimes vegetables like cucumber or carrots. It’s often garnished with sesame seeds for added flavor and texture.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-2\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>2. What are the pros and cons of eating seaweed?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Eating seaweed has several benefits, including being rich in vitamins and minerals, particularly iodine, which is essential for thyroid function. However, it can also be high in sodium and may contain heavy metals if sourced from polluted waters, so moderation is key.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-3\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>3. Can I eat seaweed salad daily?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Yes, you can enjoy seaweed salad daily, but it’s important to balance it with other foods. While seaweed is nutritious, consuming it in moderation helps avoid excessive iodine intake and ensures a varied diet.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div id=\"faq-question-4\" class=\"rank-math-list-item\">\n<h3 class=\"rank-math-question \"><strong>4. What does seaweed do for your body?</strong></h3>\n<div class=\"rank-math-answer \">\n\n<p>Seaweed is packed with nutrients that can support overall health. It provides antioxidants, aids digestion, and can help regulate metabolism. Additionally, its high fiber content can promote gut health and keep you feeling full longer.</p>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"final-thoughts\"><strong>Final Thoughts</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Now that you have this easy seaweed salad recipe in your back pocket, it’s time to dive in! This vibrant dish is not only a breeze to whip up but also a delightful way to add a touch of the ocean to your table. Enjoy every bite, and don’t forget to share it with friends—after all, good food is meant to be savored together!</p>\n",
